  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1241 PM CDT Sun Jul 5 2026\n\nUpper level ridge takes hold again for the rest of the week, with\nhot and dry conditions returning. Afternoon highs climbing back to\nnear or above the 100 degree mark through Friday expected. Upper\nridge does eventually become a little more centered over the\nwestern US across Utah and Wyoming, shifting a little farther away\nfrom the Southern Plains. Low level moisture will remain in place\nand with a little cooler mid level temperatures with the northwest\nflow aloft, and thus a little less capping, getting some at least\nisolated diurnal showers and storms next week looks possible. \nSome attempt at a weak upper level low developing again as well, \nwhich would only help rain chances. Temperatures likely to fall a \nfew degrees as well, both from the afternoon cu field developing \nand from the ridge being a little farther away.",
